[Please explain how you would play your favorite board game or card game.] I think a good card game that we like to play is called Thirty-one. We played this all through our lives, even going back to kids, and I remember our aunts and uncles playing it. You deal out three cards to everyone around the table. And then you put down the deck and flip one over. And then as you pass from player to player, they have the option of picking up the top card (and) or picking off the draw pile. The object of the game is to get thirty-one in your hand. But you can also knock. And if you knock, everyone else has (a p-) one more play. And then everyone puts their hand down. And the lowest score of the same suit loses and you have to pay into the pot.
