[Please explain the steps to change a tire on a car.] Please explain the steps to change a tire on a car. Well you have to assume you got a spare tire. You better check it before you start doing anything else. And you need to find a jack and a jack handle and a lug wrench. Start by loosening the lug wrench before you (bu-) jack the car up. Look and see if the car has any special places underneath of it to put the jack. (some) Some do, especially foreign cars. And jack the car up safely. It's a good idea before you jack it up though to (ja-) to chalk the wheels. Make sure you put the car in park. Unscrew the (uh) lug nuts. Put them in the hub cap. That's a good place to keep 'em. And then take the tire off. And you may have to jack it up a little bit further to put the new tire on because the new tire will be tall because it's full of air. Put the (nug lug nuts) lug nuts back on and tighten them up in an alternating pattern. (If you have) Just one across from the other. Don't tighten them up all in a row. (Go arou-) Go around (the car) tire several times to make sure you got it good and tight and that it is balanced. (Then I g-) Then you get your car (you you your) your spare tire. You need your blown tire fixed and then you have a spare (a-) again.
