[Please explain how you would play your favorite board game or card game.] One of my favorite card games is Spite and Malice. You take one deck of cards for each person playing. You shuffle then all up. You deal out fifteen cards for (a) a pot for each player that they have to reserve to the side. And then you (hand out five) deal out five cards to each member. The person with an ace starts. And they put the ace down in the center between the two extra piles of cards that were not shuffled out and dealt. Then it proceeds until you build on those piles. You can have up to four of them in the center starting with an ace. And you work up to (a) a king. And when you're done, that's removed and you can start a new pile. Again only four piles can be there. You try to see who's the first one done with their reserve pile of fifteen cards. It's great fun and sometimes very frustrating.
