[Please explain the steps to change a tire on a car.] Open the trunk, if that's where the spare tire is located. Take the nut off the spare tire. And remove the spare tire from the car and put it on the ground next to the flat tire. (From b-) Where the spare tire came from, there should be a jack of some kind. Put it together and attach the long handle. Move back to the flat tire and take off the hub cap if there is one. Then attach the jack to the little slot that's shown (on the) in the owner's manual and (um) just get it snug. Then loosen, just loosen (the nut) the lug nuts that are on the wheel. Then jack it up so that the wheel is no longer touching the ground and leaves enough clearance for a new tire to go on. Take the lug nuts off all the way. Remove the wheel. Put it on the ground. Put the new wheel on. Put the lug nuts on. (um) Tighten them as best you can. (um) When the tire's in the air sometimes it spins. (um) Tighten 'em using an opposite pattern for each nut. And then (um) lower the jack and really snug them hard. Put the (uh) jack and the (bro-) broken tire back where the spare came from and (um) take it to your dealership to get (the sp-) the tire fixed.
