[Tell us about a hobby that doesn’t make much sense to you.] Perhaps golf is a hobby that does not make much sense to me, for I see very few happy people out on the golf course. They hit the ball and chase it if they can find it, if it's not in a sand trap or in a water trap. It seems that people who play a lot of golf are very emphatic about the game, but you hit a ball, chase it, and hit it again. Doesn't seem to make a lot of sense. I understand a lot of skill is required to play golf well. However, for most people, it's hit the ball and chase it. I can hit a golf ball a long ways, but I can't always see where it went, so I need people with me as spotters to watch where the ball goes so I can find it for a second hit. Of course, I guess the solution to that would be a hole in one, which I've only done once in my life, and that was on a course that was under construction, so the hole was shorter than usual.
