[Please explain the steps to make your favorite sandwich or other lunch food.] So my favorite sandwich to make is a grilled cheese sandwich. (um) Pretty easy, I will usually butter two slices of bread on one side. I'll put the first slice of bread down into a hot skillet. (um) While it's cooking, I'll put a slice of American cheese on top and then I'll go ahead and put the top layer of the bread on the sandwich. I wait about a minute or so until the one side has a good (brown um) browning on it. And then I'll flip it over. And then once I flip it over, I'll let it cook another thirty seconds to a minute or until the bottom of that side of the bread is (um) browned as well. Doesn't take a whole lot of time and it ends up tasting amazing. I know a lot of people will use mayo instead of butter, but I prefer butter. (um) I think it does a good job. And then I usually will make a (s-) cup of tomato soup. And I will dip that grilled cheese into the tomato soup. And that is the best lunch you could have on a cold winter's day. Love it.
