[Please explain how you would play your favorite board game or card game.] My favorite card game is Bridge. It requires four experienced players and a deck of cards. Fifty-two cards, and four suits, and thirteen different numbers. One person is the dealer and deals all the fifty-two cards out. So each of us has thirteen cards. We value the hand in a way that involves giving an ace four points, a king three, a queen two, a jack one, and some points for how the suits are distributed in the hand. And then we take turns making a bid, which is essentially a promise as to how many of the tricks we expect to take. A trick is one card from each player, and the highest value card on the trick wins the trick. There's lots more to the game, but it's too complicated to explain to someone who hasn't already played it.
