[Please explain how you would play your favorite board game or card game.] My favorite card game is Blackjack. With Blackjack there's a dealer and several players. The dealer deals two cards to each player, two cards to himself. The idea is to get the highest score you can get without getting more than twenty-one points. If you get more than twenty-one points, you lose. If you get (lower) fewer points than the dealer gets, you lose. After you're dealt your two cards, you can look at your cards (and) and add up the numbers to see what your score is. The numbers two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight and nine score the same number of points (as the) as the name on the card. The ace will either be scored as one point or eleven points, depending on your choice. The ten, jack, queen, and king are each (count) count for ten points. So you can get twenty-one points with a king and an ace. You get twenty-one points if you get a king (and and a t-) and a ten, (and you and you) and you'll tell the dealer you want one more card, and (if) if it happens to be an ace, that would be twenty-one and you win. So you can ask for as many cards as you want from the dealer until you break twenty-one, or until you decide you have enough.
