[Please explain the steps to making breakfast for 4 people.] When I make breakfast for four people, I like to have a cheese omelet, and toast, and tea. So I would usually start by boiling water for the tea and put a warm teapot out with a teabag in it. And then I scramble probably six eggs together and grate, usually a cheddar cheese. Maybe a little bit of chopped garlic to go in with that. (um) Maybe a little bit of herbs de Provence mix. And I mix those in with a little bit of milk and scramble them all together. I turn on a frying pan fairly low and put some butter in to melt because butter makes it better. I put the toast in the toaster. I set the table first so that everything would be on the table and ready. And then I pour the egg mix into the frying pan. Wait for it to be partly cooked. Sprinkle the grated cheese on top of it. Fold half of the omelet over. Cover it for a minute or so. Put it on a hot plate to add to the things on the table. (uh) Put some fresh fruit on the table. Put the toast out and pour the tea in the cups. And we all sit down to eat breakfast.
