[Talk about a favorite holiday tradition.] Talk about a favorite holiday tradition. One (tram-) tradition I remember as a small child is going to the Christmas children's program at the church that my parents went to. It was a denomination that our family had gone to from my parents, to my grandparents, to my great grandparents, although it wasn't at the same exact church, it was the same denomination. And after weeks of practice during the Sunday school hour, we were to put on a children's program during the evening service. We'd all be lined up downstairs waiting anxiously for our turn to go upstairs and perform our part and then be led back downstairs. When we were done with the program, we were each given a paper brown sack. In the sack were a few nuts, usually an orange, and few bits of candy. And although it wasn't very much, it was more than I'd had for a whole month of December. And I (r-) anxiously awaited the yearly treat and savored it and kept it.
